.TH std::atomic_ref::operator= 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::atomic_ref::operator= \- std::atomic_ref::operator=

.SH Synopsis
value_type operator=( value_type desired ) const noexcept; \fB(1)\fP (constexpr since C++26)
atomic_ref& operator=( const atomic_ref& ) = delete;       \fB(2)\fP

1) Equivalent to store(desired); return desired;. This overload participates in overload
resolution only if std::is_const_v<T> is false.
2) atomic_ref is not CopyAssignable.

.SH Parameters

desired - value to assign

.SH Return value

As described above.

.SH Notes

Unlike most assignment operators, the assignment operator for atomic_ref does not return a
reference to its left-hand argument. It returns a copy of the stored value instead.

